{"name":"Pre-Raphaelite","hex":"#8b7f7a","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Pre-Raphaelite","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of or pertaining to the style called Pre-Raphaelitism."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A member of the Pre-Raphaelite Brotherhood, the group that founded the artistic movement.","One who favors or practices art as it was before Raphael; one who favors or advocates Pre-Raphaelitism."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Pre-Raphaelite"}],"entries":[{"title":"Pre-Raphaelite Brotherhood","blocks":[{"text":"The Pre-Raphaelite Brotherhood  (PRB), later known as the Pre-Raphaelites, was a group of English painters, poets, and art critics, founded in 1848 by William Holman Hunt, John Everett Millais, Dante Gabriel Rossetti, William Michael Rossetti, James Collinson, Frederic George Stephens and Thomas Woolner who formed a seven-member \"Brotherhood\" partly modelled on the Nazarene movement. The Brotherhood was only ever a loose association and their principles were shared by other artists and poets of the time, including Algernon Charles Swinburne, William Morris, Ford Madox Brown, Arthur Hughes and Marie Spartali Stillman. Later followers of the principles of the Brotherhood included Edward Burne-Jones and John William Waterhouse."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/46/William_Holman_Hunt_-_The_Hireling_Shepherd.jpg/330px-William_Holman_Hunt_-_The_Hireling_Shepherd.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pre-Raphaelite_Brotherhood","wikidata":"Q184814"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/37/Dante_Gabriel_Rossetti_-_Proserpine_-_Google_Art_Project.jpg/500px-Dante_Gabriel_Rossetti_-_Proserpine_-_Google_Art_Project.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/37/Dante_Gabriel_Rossetti_-_Proserpine_-_Google_Art_Project.jpg/500px-Dante_Gabriel_Rossetti_-_Proserpine_-_Google_Art_Project.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Proserpine, 1874, by Dante Gabriel Rossetti, with Jane Morris as model","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ADante_Gabriel_Rossetti_-_Proserpine_-_Google_Art_Project.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fb/Ford_Madox_Brown_-_The_Last_of_England_-_Google_Art_Project.jpg/500px-Ford_Madox_Brown_-_The_Last_of_England_-_Google_Art_Project.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fb/Ford_Madox_Brown_-_The_Last_of_England_-_Google_Art_Project.jpg/1280px-Ford_Madox_Brown_-_The_Last_of_England_-_Google_Art_Project.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fb/Ford_Madox_Brown_-_The_Last_of_England_-_Google_Art_Project.jpg/500px-Ford_Madox_Brown_-_The_Last_of_England_-_Google_Art_Project.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Ford Madox Brown, The Last of England depicting an emigrating couple, 1855","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AFord_Madox_Brown_-_The_Last_of_England_-_Google_Art_Project.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7b/John_Everett_Millais_-_Christ_in_the_House_of_His_Parents_%28%60The_Carpenter%27s_Shop%27%29_-_Google_Art_Project.jpg/500px-John_Everett_Millais_-_Christ_in_the_House_of_His_Parents_%28%60The_Carpenter%27s_Shop%27%29_-_Google_Art_Project.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7b/John_Everett_Millais_-_Christ_in_the_House_of_His_Parents_%28%60The_Carpenter%27s_Shop%27%29_-_Google_Art_Project.jpg/1280px-John_Everett_Millais_-_Christ_in_the_House_of_Hi